                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.34119/278: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-13T18:00:00-03:00">November 13, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:21 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>274. Braden<anchor n="11" xml:id="d189-f1"/> arrived this afternoon.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d189-f1" n="11" xml:id="d189-f1-content">
                <p>Spruille Braden, additional U. S. delegate to the Chaco Peace Conference.</p>
